## Current disposition

The course support desk's **engineering update**, read on 28 October 2026, states **#4471 closed 05 oct**:

- **Parser — fixed:** `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. [Engineering ticket 1](https://github.com/jwest/mega_dev_challange/issues/1) is closed as completed.
- **Hint — won't fix:** `booking-v3 form retired`. [Engineering ticket 2](https://github.com/jwest/mega_dev_challange/issues/2) is closed as not planned. The hint was not fixed; retiring the form removed the affected path.

This new record updates the disposition in [0002: Separate causes behind #4471](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) without editing that accepted decision. Its cause-aware triage rule still replaces [0001: subject-only merging](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject). The old incident's “known, one fix queued” text is historical, not the current status.

## Historical report coverage

The components below describe the supplied **4 October export**, before the engineering update. They do not measure post-fix failures. In particular, the table's “no ticket of its own” label describes the old export; the hint now has the linked ticket and explicit won't-fix disposition above.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Counts come from report IDs, tenant locale, form version and channel, not browser-based intake tags. Export pages overlap; one ID means one report. The shared parser and booking-v3's misleading month-first hint are separate defects. Fixing the parser is not evidence that the hint was fixed.

## Residual evidence

Five historical parser-routed reports have bodies that do not prove a day/month swap. Preserve them for follow-up; the engineering update does not establish their individual root causes or prove they were resolved. Investigate timestamps, timezone, intended dates and booking history rather than inventing a timezone diagnosis.

<ReportExceptions />

## Received versus merged

Reports arrived from April onward. The July merge spike is backlog processing, not the start of the failures. The export continues through early October; it does not show whether any reports arrived after the 5 October closure.

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Triage going forward

Read the body and resolve the tenant's actual locale and form. Match established causes, not subject lines or browser-derived tags. Keep distinct causes apart; unknown tenants and contradictory symptoms need investigation. A newly reported regression after closure needs current evidence and a new or reopened issue; do not merge it blindly into a closed historical ticket. The retired booking-v3 path is not a current form-fix task.

<DedupeExplorer />

